1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,060
Five days in Seoul

2
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:05,240
ending with the city glowing from Namsan.

3
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:07,651
I’ll map all five days

4
00:00:07,651 --> 00:00:09,795
including easy day-trip choices

5
00:00:09,795 --> 00:00:12,577
and show you what to book and where to

6
00:00:12,577 --> 00:00:13,630
slow down.

7
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:16,900
Save a few hours for a slow café stop.

8
00:00:17,886 --> 00:00:21,206
Day one stays in central Seoul

9
00:00:21,206 --> 00:00:24,526
moving from the palace to traditional lanes

10
00:00:24,526 --> 00:00:27,446
small shops and an evening stream walk.

11
00:00:27,888 --> 00:00:30,308
Start early at Gyeongbokgung

12
00:00:30,308 --> 00:00:33,248
then walk through Bukchon and Anguk

13
00:00:33,248 --> 00:00:34,228
browse Insadong

14
00:00:34,228 --> 00:00:36,208
and finish beside Cheonggyecheon.

15
00:00:36,642 --> 00:00:39,982
Begin at Gyeongbokgung Palace.

16
00:00:39,982 --> 00:00:42,382
Arrive early for the grand gates and the

17
00:00:42,382 --> 00:00:45,082
changing of the guard at Gwanghwamun Gate.

18
00:00:45,612 --> 00:00:48,672
Hanbok wearers get free palace entry

19
00:00:48,672 --> 00:00:51,152
and rental shops are near the station.

20
00:00:51,152 --> 00:00:53,412
The palace is closed on Tuesdays

21
00:00:53,412 --> 00:00:54,872
so swap days if needed.

22
00:00:55,278 --> 00:00:58,578
Walk north into Bukchon’s traditional lanes

23
00:00:58,578 --> 00:01:01,278
then toward Anguk for a café break.

24
00:01:01,278 --> 00:01:03,758
Keep your visit unhurried and remember people

25
00:01:03,758 --> 00:01:04,518
live here.

26
00:01:04,992 --> 00:01:09,012
Continue to Insadong for craft shops and tea houses.

27
00:01:09,012 --> 00:01:11,212
It is an easy place to browse without planning

28
00:01:11,212 --> 00:01:13,352
a long list of individual stops.

29
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:16,639
End with a walk along Cheonggyecheon.

30
00:01:16,639 --> 00:01:19,624
This streamside path gives you a calmer change

31
00:01:19,624 --> 00:01:22,530
of pace after a day among busy streets.

32
00:01:22,908 --> 00:01:26,008
Day two runs from a market breakfast to

33
00:01:26,008 --> 00:01:27,768
shopping and street food

34
00:01:27,768 --> 00:01:30,808
then finishes with a sunset view from Namsan.

35
00:01:31,278 --> 00:01:33,138
Start at Gwangjang Market

36
00:01:33,138 --> 00:01:35,778
head to Myeongdong for the afternoon

37
00:01:35,778 --> 00:01:38,958
and go up to N Seoul Tower for sunset.

38
00:01:39,384 --> 00:01:43,984
Have breakfast at Gwangjang Market and try bindaetteok

39
00:01:43,984 --> 00:01:46,284
a mung bean pancake.

40
00:01:46,284 --> 00:01:47,384
Browse the stalls

41
00:01:47,384 --> 00:01:49,904
then leave room for more snacks later.

42
00:01:50,898 --> 00:01:53,858
Spend the afternoon among Myeongdong’s shops

43
00:01:53,858 --> 00:01:55,426
and street-food stalls.

44
00:01:55,426 --> 00:01:57,516
It is a good place to pause

45
00:01:57,516 --> 00:02:00,718
snack and take the day at your own pace.

46
00:02:01,068 --> 00:02:04,788
Head to N Seoul Tower for sunset and the

47
00:02:04,788 --> 00:02:05,988
city lights.

48
00:02:05,988 --> 00:02:08,008
If you want to visit an observatory

49
00:02:08,008 --> 00:02:10,508
book ahead and check the current details.

50
00:02:10,926 --> 00:02:14,826
Day three explores west Seoul:

51
00:02:14,826 --> 00:02:18,426
relaxed cafés and a railway park first

52
00:02:18,426 --> 00:02:20,286
lively Hongdae next

53
00:02:20,286 --> 00:02:22,786
then an evening by the Han River.

54
00:02:23,232 --> 00:02:24,821
Start in Yeonnam-dong

55
00:02:24,821 --> 00:02:26,348
walk through Hongdae

56
00:02:26,348 --> 00:02:29,464
then choose Mangwon or Yeouido Hangang Park

57
00:02:29,464 --> 00:02:31,292
for your river stop.

58
00:02:31,602 --> 00:02:35,308
Yeonnam-dong is known for relaxed cafés and a

59
00:02:35,308 --> 00:02:38,328
long park along an old railway line.

60
00:02:38,328 --> 00:02:41,922
Take time here before heading next door.

61
00:02:42,372 --> 00:02:45,452
Hongdae is Seoul’s university area

62
00:02:45,452 --> 00:02:47,172
with street performers

63
00:02:47,172 --> 00:02:48,892
shops and nightlife.

64
00:02:48,892 --> 00:02:49,592
Wander the streets

65
00:02:49,592 --> 00:02:52,612
and stay for dinner if the energy suits you.

66
00:02:53,286 --> 00:02:54,686
Before dinner

67
00:02:54,686 --> 00:02:57,786
go to Mangwon or Yeouido Hangang Park.

68
00:02:57,786 --> 00:03:00,366
Yeouido has river cruises after dark

69
00:03:00,366 --> 00:03:03,566
and locals often order fried chicken to the riverbank.

70
00:03:03,984 --> 00:03:07,704
Day four is your modern Seoul day:

71
00:03:07,704 --> 00:03:08,984
converted factories

72
00:03:08,984 --> 00:03:10,344
a giant library

73
00:03:10,344 --> 00:03:13,304
and a high city view before a lakeside walk.

74
00:03:13,602 --> 00:03:16,202
Begin in Seongsu

75
00:03:16,202 --> 00:03:18,842
cross the river to COEX in Gangnam

76
00:03:18,842 --> 00:03:22,462
then end in Jamsil at Lotte World Tower and

77
00:03:22,462 --> 00:03:23,522
Seokchon Lake.

78
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:27,770
Seongsu-dong is an old factory district turned

79
00:03:27,770 --> 00:03:28,694
into cafés

80
00:03:28,694 --> 00:03:30,808
concept stores and pop-ups.

81
00:03:30,808 --> 00:03:34,506
Nearby Seoul Forest makes this a good place to

82
00:03:34,506 --> 00:03:35,664
slow down.

83
00:03:36,006 --> 00:03:40,006
Cross the river to COEX mall in Gangnam and

84
00:03:40,006 --> 00:03:42,586
see its giant library.

85
00:03:42,586 --> 00:03:44,466
Keep this stop simple:

86
00:03:44,466 --> 00:03:45,686
browse the space

87
00:03:45,686 --> 00:03:46,406
take a break

88
00:03:46,406 --> 00:03:47,566
and move on.

89
00:03:47,856 --> 00:03:51,816
Finish at Lotte World Tower in Jamsil.

90
00:03:51,816 --> 00:03:54,976
Seoul Sky has one of the city’s best night views;

91
00:03:54,976 --> 00:03:57,916
Seokchon Lake is lovely for a walk nearby.

92
00:03:58,266 --> 00:04:01,266
Want a calmer day?

93
00:04:01,266 --> 00:04:04,626
Swap Gangnam for Changdeokgung and its Secret Garden

94
00:04:04,626 --> 00:04:07,466
which is visited by guided tour.

95
00:04:07,466 --> 00:04:08,246
Book ahead

96
00:04:08,246 --> 00:04:10,366
then finish at a Korean bathhouse.

97
00:04:10,884 --> 00:04:12,684
For the last day

98
00:04:12,684 --> 00:04:14,664
choose one trip beyond Seoul.

99
00:04:14,664 --> 00:04:17,684
The best fit depends on whether you want history

100
00:04:17,684 --> 00:04:18,444
island walks

101
00:04:18,444 --> 00:04:21,164
a guided visit or an easy city outing.

102
00:04:21,534 --> 00:04:23,594
Here are four options

103
00:04:23,594 --> 00:04:26,574
not four stops to squeeze into one day.

104
00:04:26,574 --> 00:04:27,394
Pick one

105
00:04:27,394 --> 00:04:29,174
then check transport and any booking

106
00:04:29,174 --> 00:04:30,914
requirements before you go.

107
00:04:31,344 --> 00:04:35,044
The DMZ is the most unusual choice

108
00:04:35,044 --> 00:04:38,164
but visits are by organised tour only.

109
00:04:38,164 --> 00:04:40,224
Bring your passport and book ahead.

110
00:04:40,698 --> 00:04:44,478
Suwon is the easiest option to do on your own.

111
00:04:44,478 --> 00:04:46,198
Walk along Hwaseong Fortress

112
00:04:46,198 --> 00:04:48,978
about an hour away by subway or train

113
00:04:48,978 --> 00:04:51,878
then find fried chicken near the market.

114
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:55,780
Choose Nami Island for walks by the river.

115
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:57,920
It is especially appealing in autumn

116
00:04:57,920 --> 00:05:00,200
when the island’s scenery is at its best.

117
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:04,530
Incheon is handy if you fly out the next day.

118
00:05:04,530 --> 00:05:05,970
Visit Chinatown and Songdo

119
00:05:05,970 --> 00:05:08,290
and make the most of a day that also

120
00:05:08,290 --> 00:05:09,630
keeps you near the airport.

121
00:05:10,128 --> 00:05:14,348
The subway reaches every stop on this plan.

122
00:05:14,348 --> 00:05:17,028
Get a transit card when you arrive;

123
00:05:17,028 --> 00:05:18,888
transfers between subway and bus are

124
00:05:18,888 --> 00:05:20,608
discounted when you use one.

125
00:05:21,234 --> 00:05:26,074
Taxis are good value for late nights or short hops.

126
00:05:26,074 --> 00:05:28,354
Use a Korean map app to plan routes and

127
00:05:28,354 --> 00:05:30,114
show the driver your destination.

128
00:05:30,636 --> 00:05:32,856
For a central base

129
00:05:32,856 --> 00:05:34,496
look at Myeongdong

130
00:05:34,496 --> 00:05:36,536
Jongno or City Hall.

131
00:05:36,536 --> 00:05:39,376
Hongdae also suits travelers who want nightlife.

132
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:42,390
Do the busiest sights early

133
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:44,370
then keep evenings for markets

134
00:05:44,370 --> 00:05:46,270
the river and night views.

135
00:05:46,270 --> 00:05:49,050
That rhythm helps the five days feel relaxed.

136
00:05:49,512 --> 00:05:52,832
Book ahead for a DMZ tour

137
00:05:52,832 --> 00:05:57,132
the Secret Garden tour and observatories at sunset.

138
00:05:57,132 --> 00:05:59,072
Check current details before you go.

139
00:05:59,418 --> 00:06:00,703
Three easy mistakes:

140
00:06:00,703 --> 00:06:03,005
arriving late at the busiest sights

141
00:06:03,005 --> 00:06:04,932
forgetting palace closing days

142
00:06:04,932 --> 00:06:07,769
and trying to fit every day-trip choice into

143
00:06:07,769 --> 00:06:08,658
one day.

144
00:06:09,228 --> 00:06:12,108
Gyeongbokgung closes Tuesdays

145
00:06:12,108 --> 00:06:15,868
and Changdeokgung closes Mondays.

146
00:06:15,868 --> 00:06:16,808
Swap your days if needed

147
00:06:16,808 --> 00:06:21,448
and leave a little free time for cafés and wandering.

148
00:06:22,182 --> 00:06:25,142
Is five days enough for Seoul?

149
00:06:25,142 --> 00:06:26,182
Yes.

150
00:06:26,182 --> 00:06:28,062
You can cover the main sights

151
00:06:28,062 --> 00:06:31,062
several neighborhoods and a day trip without rushing.

152
00:06:31,584 --> 00:06:33,744
Where should you stay?

153
00:06:33,744 --> 00:06:35,164
Choose somewhere central

154
00:06:35,164 --> 00:06:36,644
such as Myeongdong

155
00:06:36,644 --> 00:06:37,884
Jongno or City Hall

156
00:06:37,884 --> 00:06:40,444
so most days begin with a short ride.

157
00:06:40,986 --> 00:06:43,766
What is the best day trip?

158
00:06:43,766 --> 00:06:46,726
The DMZ is the most unusual

159
00:06:46,726 --> 00:06:48,806
Suwon is easiest on your own

160
00:06:48,806 --> 00:06:51,246
and Nami Island is best in autumn.

161
00:06:51,636 --> 00:06:53,056
Five days:

162
00:06:53,056 --> 00:06:55,796
palace lanes and the stream; market

163
00:06:55,796 --> 00:06:57,516
Myeongdong and Namsan;

164
00:06:57,516 --> 00:06:59,076
Hongdae and the river;

165
00:06:59,076 --> 00:07:00,116
modern Seoul;

166
00:07:00,116 --> 00:07:01,456
then one day trip.

167
00:07:01,854 --> 00:07:02,819
The full guide

168
00:07:02,819 --> 00:07:05,004
with maps and links for every stop

169
00:07:05,004 --> 00:07:07,087
is free at Korea Plainly dot com.

170
00:07:07,087 --> 00:07:09,729
The link is at the top of the description.

171
00:07:09,729 --> 00:07:10,695
If this helped

172
00:07:10,695 --> 00:07:12,219
subscribe for more plain

173
00:07:12,219 --> 00:07:14,094
practical guides to Korea.

